## Data Models

Location: [src/models/](file:///c:/Users/teddy/projects/workout-app/src/models)

Models are **TypeScript interfaces** - they define the *shape* of your data without any logic. Think of them as blueprints.

### Core Models

````carousel
### Exercise ([exercise.ts](file:///c:/Users/teddy/projects/workout-app/src/models/exercise.ts))

The definition of an exercise (e.g., "Bench Press", "Squat").

```typescript
interface Exercise {
    id: string;
    name: string;                    // "Bench Press"
    category: ExerciseCategory;      // 'chest', 'back', 'legs', etc.
    muscleGroups: MuscleContribution[]; // Which muscles, with percentages
    equipment: Equipment[];          // Barbell, dumbbell, machine, etc.
    trackWeight: boolean;            // Does this exercise track weight?
    trackReps: boolean;              // Does it track reps?
    trackTime: boolean;              // Does it track duration? (for planks, etc.)
    isCustom: boolean;               // User-created?
    isFavorite: boolean;
    isHidden: boolean;
}
```

**Key insight:** An Exercise is a *definition*, not an actual workout. It's like a recipe, not a meal.
<!-- slide -->
### Workout ([workout.ts](file:///c:/Users/teddy/projects/workout-app/src/models/workout.ts))

An actual workout session the user logs.

```typescript
interface Workout {
    id: string;
    name: string;                    // "Morning Push Day"
    status: 'in_progress' | 'completed' | 'abandoned';
    
    // Sections (only main is required)
    warmup: WorkoutSection | null;
    main: WorkoutSection;            // Contains the exercises
    cooldown: WorkoutSection | null;
    
    // Timing
    startedAt: Date;
    completedAt: Date | null;
    totalDuration: number | null;
    
    // Stats (calculated when saved)
    totalVolume: number | null;      // weight × reps
    totalSets: number | null;
}
```

A Workout contains **WorkoutExercises**, which contain **WorkoutSets**. This is the hierarchy:
```
Workout
└── WorkoutSection (main)
    └── WorkoutExercise[] (each exercise you perform)
        └── WorkoutSet[] (each set within that exercise)
```
<!-- slide -->
### Template ([template.ts](file:///c:/Users/teddy/projects/workout-app/src/models/template.ts))

A saved workout structure you can reuse.

```typescript
interface Template {
    id: string;
    name: string;                    // "Push Day A"
    exercises: TemplateExercise[];   // The exercises in this template
    exerciseCount: number;
    lastUsedAt: Date | null;
    useCount: number;
    isFavorite: boolean;
}
```

**Relationship:** You start a workout FROM a template. The template defines which exercises; the workout records what you actually did.
<!-- slide -->
### Split ([split.ts](file:///c:/Users/teddy/projects/workout-app/src/models/split.ts))

A training program - a sequence of templates over days.

```typescript
interface Split {
    id: string;
    name: string;                    // "Push/Pull/Legs"
    schedule: SplitScheduleItem[];   // Day 1: Push, Day 2: Pull, etc.
    isBuiltIn: boolean;              // Pre-made split vs. user-created
    isFavorite: boolean;
}

interface SplitScheduleItem {
    dayIndex: number;                // 0, 1, 2, ...
    templateId: string | null;       // null = rest day
}
```

**Example:** A PPL split might have:
- Day 0: Push template
- Day 1: Pull template  
- Day 2: Legs template
- Day 3: Rest (templateId = null)
- ...repeat
````

