## Services

Location: [src/services/](file:///c:/Users/teddy/projects/workout-app/src/services)

Services handle **database operations**. They're the only layer that talks to SQLite.

### Service Pattern

Every service follows the same pattern:

```typescript
export async function saveWorkout(workout: Workout): Promise<void> {
    const db = await getDatabase();
    if (!db) {
        console.log('Database not available (Expo Go mode)');
        return;  // Graceful degradation
    }
    
    await db.withTransactionAsync(async () => {
        // Insert workout
        // Insert exercises
        // Insert sets
    });
}
```

**Key patterns:**
1. **Get database connection** (may be null in Expo Go)
2. **Return empty/gracefully** if no DB
3. **Use transactions** for multi-table writes
4. **Hydrate** when reading (convert DB rows → TypeScript objects)

### Service Responsibilities

| Service | Purpose |
|---------|---------|
| [database.ts](file:///c:/Users/teddy/projects/workout-app/src/services/database.ts) | DB connection, schema creation |
| [workoutService.ts](file:///c:/Users/teddy/projects/workout-app/src/services/workoutService.ts) | Save/load workout history |
| [templateService.ts](file:///c:/Users/teddy/projects/workout-app/src/services/templateService.ts) | CRUD for templates |
| [splitService.ts](file:///c:/Users/teddy/projects/workout-app/src/services/splitService.ts) | Split management, current position tracking |
| [exerciseService.ts](file:///c:/Users/teddy/projects/workout-app/src/services/exerciseService.ts) | Exercise library, favorites, hiding |

### Barrel Export

[services/index.ts](file:///c:/Users/teddy/projects/workout-app/src/services/index.ts) re-exports everything so other code can:

```typescript
import { saveWorkout, getTemplates, getActiveSplit } from '../services';
```

Instead of importing from 5 different files.

