## State Management

Location: [src/stores/workoutStore.ts](file:///c:/Users/teddy/projects/workout-app/src/stores/workoutStore.ts)

### What is Zustand?

Zustand is a lightweight state management library. Think of it as a "global variable" that:
- Any component can read
- Any component can update
- Automatically re-renders components when it changes

### The Workout Store

```typescript
interface WorkoutState {
    // The actual data
    activeWorkout: Workout | null;
    restTimerDuration: number;
    restTimerRemaining: number;
    restTimerActive: boolean;
    
    // Actions (functions to modify state)
    startWorkout: (name?: string) => void;
    finishWorkout: () => Workout | null;
    addExercise: (exercise: Exercise) => void;
    removeExercise: (exerciseId: string) => void;
    addSet: (exerciseId: string) => void;
    completeSet: (exerciseId: string, setId: string) => void;
    startRestTimer: (seconds?: number) => void;
    // ... more
}
```

### How Components Use It

```typescript
function ExerciseCard() {
    // Subscribe to specific parts of state
    const { activeWorkout, addSet, removeSet } = useWorkoutStore();
    
    // When you call addSet(), the store updates,
    // and this component automatically re-renders
}
```

### Why Not Just Services?

- **Services** = persistent storage (database)
- **Store** = current session state (RAM)

When you're logging a workout, changes go to the **Store**. When you finish, the workout is saved via **Services** to the database.

