## Components

Location: [src/components/](file:///c:/Users/teddy/projects/workout-app/src/components)

Components are **reusable UI building blocks**. They're like LEGO pieces.

### Component Hierarchy

```
ExerciseCard
├── SetRow (repeated for each set)
│   └── (weight input, reps input, complete button)
└── ActiveRestLine (shown when rest timer is active)

ExercisePicker (modal)
└── (search, filters, exercise list)

WorkoutKeyboard
└── (custom numeric keyboard for weight/reps)
```

### Props Pattern

Components receive data and callbacks via **props**:

```typescript
interface ExerciseCardProps {
    workoutExercise: WorkoutExercise;  // Data to display
    onAddSet: () => void;              // Function to call when "+ Add Set" tapped
    onRemoveExercise: () => void;      // Function to call when "×" tapped
    onCompleteSet: (setId: string) => void;
}

function ExerciseCard({ workoutExercise, onAddSet, ... }: ExerciseCardProps) {
    // Render UI, call callbacks when user interacts
}
```

**Key insight:** Components don't know *how* to add a set—they just call `onAddSet()` and let the parent decide.

