## Screens

Location: [src/screens/](file:///c:/Users/teddy/projects/workout-app/src/screens)

Screens are **complete pages** that compose components and connect to state.

### WorkoutScreen ([WorkoutScreen.tsx](file:///c:/Users/teddy/projects/workout-app/src/screens/WorkoutScreen.tsx))

The main screen. Has two modes:

**No Active Workout:**
- Shows "Ready to workout?" hero
- Current template / split cards
- Recent workout history
- Start button

**Active Workout:**
- Elapsed timer
- List of ExerciseCards
- Custom keyboard overlay
- Finish/discard buttons

### Screen Responsibilities

```typescript
function WorkoutScreen() {
    // 1. Connect to store
    const { activeWorkout, startWorkout, addExercise } = useWorkoutStore();
    
    // 2. Local UI state (modals, etc.)
    const [showSplitsModal, setShowSplitsModal] = useState(false);
    
    // 3. Load data from services
    useEffect(() => {
        loadData();  // Fetches templates, splits, recent workouts
    }, []);
    
    // 4. Define handlers that wire everything together
    const handleFinishWorkout = async () => {
        const workout = await finishWorkout();
        await saveWorkout(workout);  // Persist to DB
        await loadData();            // Refresh UI
    };
    
    // 5. Render UI
    return (
        <View>
            {activeWorkout ? (
                <ActiveWorkoutUI />
            ) : (
                <EmptyStateUI />
            )}
        </View>
    );
}
```

